  "question": {
    "text": "The energy $E$ and momentum $p$ of a moving body of mass $m$ are related by some equation. Given that c represents the speed of light, identify the correct equation"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{E}^2=\\mathrm{pc}^2+\\mathrm{m}^2 \\mathrm{c}^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{E}^2=\\mathrm{p}^2 \\mathrm{c}^2+\\mathrm{m}^2 \\mathrm{c}^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{E}^2=\\mathrm{pc}^2+\\mathrm{m}^2 \\mathrm{c}^4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{E}^2=\\mathrm{p}^2 \\mathrm{c}^2+\\mathrm{m}^2 \\mathrm{c}^4$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We need to check the dimensions only.\nWith momentum the dimension\n$E^2=p^2 C^2$\nAnd with mass $E^2=m^2 c^4$\nSo $E^2=p^2 C^2+m^2 c^4$ (dimensionally)"
  }
}